      "description": "All of the opponent's untapped creatures that could block are either a 1/1 (Amoeboid Changeling) or a 2/4 (Littjara Kinseekers). The 5/5 Kinseekers is tapped. Attacking with at least Brightmare (2/3) would likely get through for 2 damage (opponent probably blocks with the 1/1 to save the 2/4, and Brightmare survives). Even attacking with just the Chorister could force a trade with the Changeling, removing its useful tap ability.",
      "action_taken": "Did not attack with any creatures.",
      "better_line": "Attack with Brightmare (2/3). If blocked by the 1/1 Changeling, Brightmare kills it and survives — removing a useful utility creature. If blocked by the 2/4 Kinseekers, both survive but no damage is lost. Either way, attacking with Brightmare is low-risk and could deal 2 damage or trade favorably.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 222,
      "player": "Gem3P Coach",
      "decision_index": 160,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With 3 untapped Islands and no other use for the mana (Gigantoplasm costs 3U which can't be cast with only 3 Islands), declining to equip Heirloom Blade wastes mana that could boost a creature for next turn's attack. Opponent is at 5 life, so the +3/+1 from Heirloom Blade on any creature (like Universal Automaton or Bloodline Pretender) would significantly increase lethal pressure.",
      "action_taken": "Passed without equipping Heirloom Blade, wasting 3 available mana.",
      "better_line": "Equip Heirloom Blade ({1}) to Bloodline Pretender (soon to be 3/3 with counter) making it a 6/4, or to Universal Automaton making it 4/2, to maximize damage potential next turn against an opponent at 5 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 259,
      "player": "Gem3F Tinker",
      "decision_index": 191,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "At 5 life facing a 5/5 Kinseekers and 2/4 Kinseekers about to untap (plus Bloodline Pretender 3/3), attacking with ALL creatures leaves no blockers. The attack deals maybe 4-7 damage against a 19-life opponent — nowhere near lethal. Next turn the opponent can swing for 11+ damage with no blockers available except whatever Coach plays post-combat (just Emancipation Angel 3/3 flying).",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with all four creatures (Anointed Chorister, Brightmare, Voice of the Provinces, Human Token)",
      "better_line": "Attack with only Voice of the Provinces (3 unblockable flying damage) and possibly the 1/1 Human Token. Keep Brightmare and Anointed Chorister back as blockers to survive the opponent's counterattack. Post-combat, play Plains and cast Emancipation Angel for additional defense. Brightmare blocks the 5/5, Anointed Chorister can chump, and Emancipation Angel provides another body.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 265,
      "player": "Gem3P Coach",
      "decision_index": 194,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Gem3F Tinker declined to block at all, taking 7 damage and letting opponent gain 1 life from Anointed Chorister's lifelink. Bloodline Pretender 3/3 could have blocked Brightmare 2/3 for free (killing it while surviving), and Universal Automaton 1/1 could have traded with Anointed Chorister 1/1 (preventing lifelink). This allowed the opponent to keep creatures alive unnecessarily and took extra damage when the opponent is at 5 life and could use any life gain from lifelink.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to assign any blockers, taking 7 damage (19→12) and letting opponent gain 1 life (5→6).",
      "better_line": "Block Brightmare 2/3 with Bloodline Pretender 3/3 (kills Brightmare, Pretender survives) and optionally block Anointed Chorister 1/1 with Universal Automaton 1/1 (trade, deny lifelink). This reduces damage taken to 4 and kills 1-2 of opponent's creatures.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 270,
      "player": "Gem3F Tinker",
      "decision_index": 196,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "At 5 life facing lethal threats next turn (5/5 Kinseekers, 3/3 Pretender), Coach declined to activate Anointed Chorister's +3/+3 pump ability while it was attacking with lifelink. This would have dealt 3 extra damage and gained 4 life (going from 5 to 9), significantly improving survivability. Coach had exactly 5 mana available ({4}{W}) to pay for the activation.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without activating Anointed Chorister's pump ability during combat.",
      "better_line": "Activate Anointed Chorister's {4}{W} ability to give it +3/+3, making it a 4/4 lifelink attacker. This gains 4 life (critical at 5 HP) and deals 3 additional damage. The extra life could be the difference between surviving the opponent's next attack or dying.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 269,
      "player": "Gem3P Coach",
      "decision_index": 195,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Copied Littjara Kinseekers with Gigantoplasm instead of Voice of the Provinces. While copying Kinseekers gives a 3/5 (with ETB counter) + scry 1, copying Voice of the Provinces would give a 3/3 flyer + a 1/1 Human token. With the board gummed up on the ground and life totals at 12 vs 11, the flying evasion from Voice is significantly more valuable for pushing through damage. The extra token body also has synergy with Bloodline Pretender.",
      "action_taken": "Copied Littjara Kinseekers with Gigantoplasm, getting a ground 3/5 with scry 1",
      "better_line": "Copy Voice of the Provinces to get a 3/3 flyer and a 1/1 Human token, providing evasive damage to close out the game",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 316,
      "player": "Gem3F Tinker",
      "decision_index": 228,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Triple-blocked the smaller 2/4 Littjara Kinseekers with Emancipation Angel, Brightmare, and Griffin Token (massive overkill), while only chump-blocking the 5/5 with Chorister and leaving the growing 4/4 Bloodline Pretender unblocked. Same 6 damage taken either way, but killed a less valuable creature.",
      "action_taken": "Emancipation Angel + Brightmare + Griffin Token triple-block the 2/4 Kinseekers; Anointed Chorister chump-blocks the 5/5 Kinseekers. Bloodline Pretender 4/4 goes unblocked.",
      "better_line": "Emancipation Angel + Griffin Token block Bloodline Pretender 4/4 (killing it), Brightmare blocks the 2/4 Kinseekers (both survive), Anointed Chorister blocks Universal Automaton (trade). Same 6 damage taken but kills the dangerous growing 4/4 Pretender instead of a 2/4.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 328,
      "player": "Gem3P Coach",
      "decision_index": 237,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Amoeboid Changeling (1/1) is blocked by Brightmare (2/3) and Griffin Token (2/2) and will die in combat regardless. Equipping Heirloom Blade to it before damage would make it 4/2, allowing it to kill the Brightmare (assign 3 damage to Brightmare, 1 to Griffin Token). More importantly, when the equipped Changeling dies, Heirloom Blade's death trigger would let Tinker search their library for ANY creature card (since Changeling has all creature types), providing significant card advantage. The equip cost of {1} is easily affordable with 4 untapped Islands.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without equipping Heirloom Blade to the doomed Amoeboid Changeling.",
      "better_line": "Activate Heirloom Blade to equip it to Amoeboid Changeling before combat damage. This kills Brightmare instead of dealing minimal damage, and triggers Heirloom Blade's death ability to tutor a creature card from the library.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 340,
      "player": "Gem3F Tinker",
      "decision_index": 244,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Passed precombat main phase without activating Guardian Idol to make it a 2/2 creature for attacking. With most of opponent's creatures tapped, maximizing attackers is important. The 2 extra damage from Guardian Idol could be significant given the opponent is at 12 life and Coach has strong attacking potential this turn.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority in precombat main, moving to combat without activating Guardian Idol.",
      "better_line": "Activate Guardian Idol for {2} to make it a 2/2 Golem, then proceed to combat to attack with maximum force including the Idol alongside flyers and ground creatures.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 344,
      "player": "Gem3P Coach",
      "decision_index": 246,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "All of the opponent's creatures are tapped, meaning all attackers would go through unblocked. Coach attacked with only the two flyers for 5 damage instead of also sending at least the Anointed Chorister (1/1) and Human Token (1/1) which have minimal defensive value as blockers. This left 2-4 free damage on the table in a racing situation where Coach is at 8 life.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with only Voice of the Provinces and Griffin Token for 5 damage.",
      "better_line": "Attack with at least Voice of the Provinces, Griffin Token, Anointed Chorister, and Human Token for 7 damage. Could consider sending Brightmare too for 9 total, keeping Feat of Resistance for defensive tricks on the crackback.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 344,
      "player": "Gem3P Coach",
      "decision_index": 246,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Failed to equip Heirloom Blade before combat. With 8 untapped lands and equip cost of {1}, equipping the Blade to the 5/5 Kinseekers (making it 8/6) or another attacker before declaring attacks would significantly increase damage output. Against an opponent at 8 life with limited untapped blockers (Chorister 1/1, Brightmare 2/3, Human Token 1/1, and possibly Guardian Idol 2/2), a powered-up attack could be lethal or near-lethal.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority in precombat main without equipping Heirloom Blade or using any abilities.",
      "better_line": "Equip Heirloom Blade to the 5/5 Littjara Kinseekers (making it 8/6) for {1}, then attack with multiple creatures to push through lethal or near-lethal damage against the 8-life opponent.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 366,
      "player": "Gem3F Tinker",
      "decision_index": 266,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Attacking with all 5 creatures when opponent has 4 potential blockers (Brightmare, Anointed Chorister, Human Token, Guardian Idol) means likely only 1 damage gets through unblocked. Meanwhile, leaving no blockers at 7 life against an opponent who untaps Voice of the Provinces 3/3, Griffin Token 2/2, and surviving blockers presents lethal crackback (especially with Chorister's +3/+3 pump ability available).",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with all creatures including the 5/5 and 3/5 Kinseekers, leaving no blockers behind.",
      "better_line": "Keep the 5/5 Littjara Kinseekers back as a blocker to survive the crackback. Attack with the other 4 creatures - the opponent still has to make difficult blocking decisions and Tinker survives the counter-attack.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 367,
      "player": "Gem3F Tinker",
      "decision_index": 267,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Opponent is at 7 life. By passing the precombat main phase without activating Guardian Idol (making it a 2/2 creature), Coach cannot attack with it this turn. Available untapped attackers are only Chorister (1/1), Brightmare (2/3), and Human Token (1/1) for 4 power. With Guardian Idol as a 2/2, that becomes 6 power, and Feat of Resistance could add +1/+1 and protection to push through blockers for potential lethal or near-lethal damage.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority in precombat main phase without activating Guardian Idol.",
      "better_line": "Activate Guardian Idol for 2 mana to make it a 2/2 creature, then proceed to combat and attack with Chorister, Brightmare, Human Token, and Guardian Idol (6 power total). Use Feat of Resistance in combat to grant +1/+1 and protection to push damage through blockers, potentially dealing lethal 7 damage to the opponent at 7 life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 368,
      "player": "Gem3P Coach",
      "decision_index": 268,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Coach had 6 untapped lands and could activate Guardian Idol (2 mana) to create a 2/2 blocker, reducing unblocked damage from 5 to 3 (or even 2). This would leave Coach at 5 life instead of 3 life, a meaningful buffer against the opponent's Triton Shorestalker (unblockable) coming online next turn. Coach would still have 4 mana available for Feat of Resistance.",
      "action_taken": "Blocked with only Brightmare, Human Token, and Anointed Chorister, leaving 5 damage unblocked (2/4 and 3/5 Kinseekers).",
      "better_line": "Activate Guardian Idol for 2 mana to make it a 2/2, then block the 2/4 Kinseekers with it in addition to the other blocks, reducing unblocked damage to 3 and preserving 2 more life.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 371,
      "player": "Gem3P Coach",
      "decision_index": 271,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Failed to play Plains from hand before combat. While the player has 6 untapped lands already, playing a land is free and provides an extra mana that could be relevant (e.g., activating Guardian Idol + casting Feat of Resistance in the same turn requires 4 mana, leaving more flexibility). More importantly, opponent has zero available blockers (all tapped or summoning sick), so this is a lethal attack turn with Guardian Idol (2/2) + Voice of the Provinces (3/3) + Griffin Token (2/2) = 7 damage against 7 life.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority in precombat main without playing the Plains land from hand.",
      "better_line": "Play Plains first (free action, no downside), then activate Guardian Idol to make it a 2/2, proceed to combat and attack with all three creatures for exactly 7 lethal damage.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 391,
      "player": "Gem3P Coach",
      "decision_index": 282,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Opponent is at 7 life and ALL their creatures are either tapped or summoning sick, meaning nothing can block. Activating Guardian Idol (2 mana) makes it a 2/2, then attacking with Griffin Token (2/2 flying) + Voice of the Provinces (3/3 flying) + Guardian Idol (2/2) = 7 damage = exactly lethal. Coach passed priority instead of activating Guardian Idol before declaring attackers.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without activating Guardian Idol, missing lethal.",
      "better_line": "Activate Guardian Idol for {2}, then declare attackers with Griffin Token, Voice of the Provinces, and Guardian Idol for exactly 7 damage lethal.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 393,
      "player": "Gem3P Coach",
      "decision_index": 284,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Tinker declined to block while at 7 life, taking 5 damage to go to 2 life. Both Triton Shorestalker and Shaper Apprentice could legally block (summoning sickness doesn't prevent blocking), and since neither attacker has trample, blocking both would result in 0 damage taken. Going to 2 life is extremely dangerous when the opponent could have any reach or combat tricks.",
      "action_taken": "Chose not to block, taking 5 damage (7 -> 2 life).",
      "better_line": "Block Voice of the Provinces with Triton Shorestalker and Griffin Token with Shaper Apprentice. This takes 0 damage (no trample), trades Shaper Apprentice for the Griffin token, and only loses a 1/1 Shorestalker. Staying at 7 life is far safer than dropping to 2.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 396,
      "player": "Gem3F Tinker",
      "decision_index": 286,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Opponent is at 2 life with lethal attackers declared, but opponent has 2 cards in hand and 4+ untapped Islands. Passing priority without casting Feat of Resistance risks the opponent using a blue bounce spell or combat trick to survive. Feat of Resistance on Voice of the Provinces choosing protection from blue would make it unblockable by the blue summoning-sick creatures and immune to any blue removal/bounce, guaranteeing lethal.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority during combat without casting Feat of Resistance",
      "better_line": "Cast Feat of Resistance targeting Voice of the Provinces, choosing protection from blue. This guarantees it can't be bounced or blocked by blue creatures, securing the lethal attack.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 400,
      "player": "Gem3P Coach",
      "decision_index": 290,
    }
  ],
